WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.709
Good morning, John. Today has to be an update.

00:00:01.709 --> 00:00:02.720
There's just too much going on.

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:05.400
So, update in nine parts starting now:

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:09.880
Shooting The Fault in Our Stars movie is wrapping up and while I have really enjoyed this really unique

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:13.720
behind-the-scenes look from the perspective of a total noob that is you,

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:15.780
I'm kind of glad to have you back

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:18.420
'cause somebody needs to explain debt ceilings to me.

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:21.240
Part two: Subbable is doing amazingly.

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:23.080
Wheezy Waiter's on there now. Mystery Guitar Man,

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:25.420
C.G.P. Grey, Minute Physics, Beer &amp; Board Games

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:27.160
Woodworking for Mere Mortals...

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:29.160
All you woodworking fans out there?

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:33.720
Subbable for the last two months has averaged a hundred thousand dollars a month paid out to partners.

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:35.640
Three: I've been in several recent episodes

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:38.680
of Wheezy Waiter's "The Good Stuff". There's links in the description.

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:40.540
Four: I'm headed to San Franc...

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:42.560
Ugh, doorbell.

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:47.580
It was a package from Daily Grace, which is super weird. I have - I did not expect -

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:49.040
I'm trying to open this with a -

00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:52.259
staple remover. I'm just gonna stab it with a pen.

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:55.920
Oh my god, that's a really soft pen!

00:00:55.960 --> 00:00:58.440
Scissors, they were there - they were there the whole time.

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:04.160
I wonder if it's something to drink. It says, "A belated gift to say thank you for a wonderful VidCon."

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:05.280
This is amazing.

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:08.760
Oh my God. It is a drink! It's Hendrix!

00:01:09.260 --> 00:01:10.860
(Laughs)

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:12.820
I can't believe I called it.

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:14.260
Also, "You've been hazed!

00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:19.260
What a sweetheart. Anyway, as I was saying, I'm going to San Francisco for an EDU Conference at YouTube.

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:20.800
I'm excited for good ideas and things.

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:23.300
DFTBA records is going well. Here I am at the warehouse.

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:25.700
We're getting ready for Christmas and also the Lizzie Bennet Kickstarter,

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:29.340
which I'm sorry we haven't sent out yet, but at the moment there's not a lot to do.

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:31.340
We actually have a new vlog series called "The Warehouse"

00:01:31.340 --> 00:01:33.340
starring one of our warehouse workers, Matthew -

00:01:33.640 --> 00:01:39.780
he films right over here - and this is the fort he built out of overstock boxes. It's called Fort Awesome.

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:41.460
I didn't realize, but this one - these are all still signed.

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:44.360
We still have lots of signed John Green posters here.

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:45.920
Quite a while ago, I sat right here

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:49.820
and I told you about my idea for turning a Jane Austen book into a video blog series.

00:01:49.820 --> 00:01:51.420
That thing, "The Lizzie Bennet Diaries",

00:01:51.430 --> 00:01:54.089
did very well - tens of millions of views. It won an Emmy.

00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:58.680
I'm excited to sit here again and tell you that we're doing it again, this time with Jane Austen's "Emma".

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:04.380
I think that telling stories in different ways is really fascinating and we're going to continue exploring that.

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:07.700
Probably in some more new different exciting ways.

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:12.449
But you'll have to go to youtube.com/pemberleydigital to watch and see what we're up to.

00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:14.679
Thank you to all of you who love and supported the Lizzie Bennet diaries

00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:17.360
I really hope that you like "Emma Approved" as well.

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:21.880
Also John and I are helping out with the Harry Potter Alliance's Equality for the Win Indiegogo campaign.

00:02:21.880 --> 00:02:23.640
There are a bunch of really great perks.

00:02:23.649 --> 00:02:28.740
There's an excerpt from "The Price of Dawn", the fictional novel from "The Fault in Our Stars", written by John.

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:32.240
I wrote a Harry Potter fanfic called "The Womb of Requirement",

00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:34.540
which is like an origin story for the Room of Requirement.

00:02:34.540 --> 00:02:39.260
It's going to be read into like an audiobook kind of thing - by Evanna Lynch!

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:44.880
Nyah! It will be available for not very much longer, midnight, Pacific Time, Saturday.

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:48.640
So yes, there's a lot going to be on and to be honest I'm a little fret - a lot going to be on?

00:02:49.370 --> 00:02:53.620
Yep. Take on maybe a couple more responsibilities than I should occasionally.

00:02:53.620 --> 00:02:59.320
But I feel like I have like responsibility to the world, to you John, and to Nerdfighteria,

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:01.840
and I, you know, I really appreciate that

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:03.580
I have opportunities to do all these cool things

00:03:03.580 --> 00:03:04.980
and how can you say no?

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:08.580
And then sometimes you just get somebody being really nice and sending you gin.

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:12.960
Oh, Grace... More like, daily disgrace!

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:15.021
So yeah lots of stuff going on.

00:03:15.021 --> 00:03:19.100
If you're having a hard time following it, we are on whatever social network you prefer.

00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:21.180
Newly Google+!

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:24.060
I've talked about a lot of things in this video. There's links to all of them in the description.

00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:26.500
John, I'll see you on Tuesday.

00:03:27.080 --> 00:03:28.660
Katherine just got back from the dentist.

00:03:28.660 --> 00:03:30.000
How's your face?

00:03:30.460 --> 00:03:31.600
-What face?

00:03:32.360 --> 00:03:34.760
Mop mop mop mop

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:36.500
mop mop

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:38.720
-Wanna go watch a show?

00:03:38.980 --> 00:03:40.640
-Gonna eat some mashed potatoes.

00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:41.600
-Okay.

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:42.716
-Mah-poh-tah-toes.

00:03:42.716 --> 00:03:43.700
(Laughs)

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:46.450
Poh-tah-toes.

